# Backend configuration (copy to .env for local overrides)

# Port the API listens on
PORT=5000

# Path to the SQLite database file.
# Defaults to <cwd>/data/expenses.db when unset.
# DB_PATH=./data/expenses.db

# Optional single-user password gate. Leave unset to keep the API open (local
# dev / trusted LAN). When set, clients must log in and send a bearer token.
# APP_PASSWORD=change-me
# Optional signing secret for auth tokens (defaults to APP_PASSWORD if unset).
# Set this to an independent random value so a leaked token is not also a
# password oracle.
# AUTH_SECRET=some-long-random-string
# Failed logins allowed per IP per 15 minutes. Successful logins do not count,
# so normal use never trips it. Default: 10.
# AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=10

# --- Instance flags --------------------------------------------------------
# Reported publicly by GET /api/config, which is how the frontend knows what
# kind of instance it is talking to before anyone logs in. Booleans only.
#
# Public demo: the UI shows a banner saying the data is fictional and resets.
# It does NOT imply anything else — in particular it does not disable uploads.
# DEMO_MODE=false
# Receipt upload and OCR. Turn this off on any instance you point the internet
# at without a password: /api/receipts then answers 403, and the tab disappears
# from the UI. OCR is Tesseract on your own CPU, so an open endpoint is a free
# compute service for whoever finds it.
# RECEIPTS_ENABLED=true

# --- Receipt scanning (OCR) ------------------------------------------------
# OCR engine used to read receipt photos. Default: tesseract (fully offline).
# 'claude' is a documented future option (Claude Vision) — see
# src/services/receipt/index.ts.
# RECEIPT_OCR_PROVIDER=tesseract
# Tesseract languages to load (default: pol+eng). Both ship with the app —
# `npm run tessdata` stages them into ./tessdata and the Docker image bakes them
# in. Any other language is downloaded at first scan and cached.
# RECEIPT_OCR_LANGS=pol+eng
# Where receipt images are stored. Defaults to <data dir>/receipts.
# RECEIPTS_DIR=./data/receipts
# Where Tesseract caches downloaded language data. Defaults to <data dir>/tesseract.
# TESSERACT_CACHE_PATH=./data/tesseract
# For a strictly no-egress deployment, point this at a folder holding local
# *.traineddata.gz files (or plain *.traineddata) so no language data is fetched
# over the network. ./tessdata is used automatically when it covers every
# requested language; setting this makes it mandatory rather than preferred — a
# missing language then fails the scan instead of falling back to the CDN.
# TESSERACT_LANG_PATH=./tessdata
